Usage: agent-deck launch [path] [options]

Create, start, and optionally send a message to a new session in one step.
Combines: add + session start + session send

Arguments:
  [path]    Project directory (default: group default_path, then global default_path,
            then the group's most recent session path, then current directory)

Options:
  -account string
    	Named account slot (uses its per-tool config_dir; overrides AGENTDECK_ACCOUNT)
  -additional-path value
    	Additional project directory on this host (repeatable)
  -assert-done
    	Append a completion-sentinel instruction to the message (default on for -c claude)
  -auto-mode
    	Claude: --permission-mode auto for this session (persisted; requires -c claude)
  -b	Create new branch (use with --worktree)
  -c string
    	Tool/command to run (short)
  -capabilities
    	Report authoritative creation fields and host catalogs (requires --json)
  -channel value
    	Plugin channel id (can specify multiple times); requires -c claude
  -chrome
    	Claude: --chrome for this session (persisted; requires -c claude)
  -cmd string
    	Tool/command to run (e.g., 'claude' or 'codex --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox')
  -continue
    	Claude session mode 'continue' (claude -c: resume the most recent conversation in the directory); requires -c claude
  -create-dir
    	Create the project directory when it does not exist
  -effort string
    	Reasoning effort for this session (claude: low, medium, high, xhigh, max; codex: minimal, low, medium, high, xhigh)
  -extra-arg value
    	Extra claude CLI token (can specify multiple times); requires -c claude; persisted plaintext — no secrets
  -g string
    	Group path (short)
  -group string
    	Group path (defaults to parent folder)
  -hint value
    	Durable hint key=value for recall (repeatable; e.g. --hint purpose="fix flaky auth test")
  -idle-timeout string
    	Auto-stop session after this duration of no tmux output (Go duration: 30m, 1h, 24h). 0 or unset = disabled
  -inherit-group
    	Place the child in the parent session's group instead of the cwd-derived group (auto-applied for git worktree children; use this to force it for non-worktree paths)
  -inherit-telegram-env
    	Keep TELEGRAM_* env vars in the child (#1133); off by default to prevent duplicate plugin pollers
  -json
    	Output as JSON
  -location string
    	Worktree location: sibling, subdirectory, or custom path
  -m string
    	Initial message to send (short)
  -mcp value
    	MCP to attach (can specify multiple times)
  -message string
    	Initial message to send once agent is ready
  -message-file string
    	Read the initial message from a file ('-' for stdin); avoids shell quoting of long prompts
  -model string
    	Model ID/version to use for this session (claude, codex, gemini, opencode)
  -new-branch
    	Create new branch
  -no-assert-done
    	Disable the completion-sentinel instruction
  -no-channel-link
    	Disable auto-link between --plugin entries with emits_channel=true and --channel
  -no-identity
    	Do not inject the agent-deck session identity block into the harness (global default: [launch] inject_identity)
  -no-parent
    	Disable automatic parent linking
  -no-title-sync
    	Alias for --title-lock
  -no-transition-notify
    	Suppress transition event notifications to parent session
  -no-wait
    	Don't wait for agent to be ready before sending message
  -p string
    	Parent session (short)
  -parent string
    	Parent session (creates sub-session; group is cwd-derived by default — auto-inherits the parent's group for git worktree children or with --inherit-group)
  -plugin value
    	Catalog plugin to enable for this session (can specify multiple times); requires -c claude
  -q	Minimal output (short)
  -quiet
    	Minimal output
  -resume-session string
    	Claude session ID to resume
  -sandbox
    	Run session in Docker sandbox
  -sandbox-image string
    	Docker image for sandbox (overrides config default)
  -skip-permissions
    	Claude: --dangerously-skip-permissions for this session (persisted; requires -c claude)
  -startup-query string
    	Claude startup query, delivered once on initial start
  -t string
    	Session title (short)
  -tag value
    	Tag for recall (repeatable)
  -teammate-mode
    	Claude: --teammate-mode tmux for this session (persisted; requires -c claude)
  -ticket value
    	Ticket id hint (shorthand for --hint ticket=<id>)
  -title string
    	Session title (defaults to folder name; an explicit title is locked against Claude's session-name sync)
  -title-lock
    	Lock session title so Claude's session name never overrides it; implied by an explicit -t/--title (#697)
  -tmux-socket string
    	tmux -L socket name for this session (overrides [tmux].socket_name)
  -w string
    	Create session in git worktree for branch
  -why value
    	Why this session exists (shorthand for --hint why=<text>)
  -worktree string
    	Create session in git worktree for branch
  -wrapper string
    	Wrapper command (use {command} to include tool command; auto-generated when --cmd includes extra flags; a known claude/codex subcommand in --cmd runs as-is with no wrapper instead)
  -yolo
    	Enable YOLO mode for Gemini, Codex or Hermes sessions

Examples:
  agent-deck launch . -c claude
  agent-deck launch . -c codex --model gpt-5.5
  agent-deck launch . -c claude --model claude-opus-5 --effort high
  agent-deck launch . -c claude --skip-permissions --chrome --continue   # the dialog's Claude Options rows
  agent-deck launch . -c gemini --yolo --sandbox
  agent-deck launch . -c gemini --model gemini-3.1-pro-preview
  agent-deck launch . -c claude -m "Explain this codebase"
  agent-deck launch /path/to/project -t "My Agent" -c claude -g work
  agent-deck launch . -c claude --mcp memory -m "Research topic X"
  agent-deck launch . -c claude --channel plugin:telegram@user/repo -m "Listen for messages"
  agent-deck launch . -c claude -m "Fix bug" --no-wait
  agent-deck launch . -c claude --message-file task.md   # long prompt from file, no shell quoting
  agent-deck launch . -c claude -m "Refactor X"   # auto-appends completion sentinel (see session children)
  agent-deck launch . -c "codex --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox"
  agent-deck launch . -g ard --no-parent -c claude -m "Run review"
  agent-deck launch . -c claude -w feature/new -b -m "Start work"
